{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Do not profane your daughter, etc.</b> Meaning: the El commands one who has a daughter not to conduct himself with her in a profane manner, to display her before everyone and negotiate her display before them — but rather, ״the king's daughter is all glorious within״ (Psalms 45:14). And even if his intention is for the benefit of her marriage, so that it becomes known that she is a beautiful and pleasant girl and she will be married to one worthy of her — despite all this, the El commands, for it is a profanation of her, and the outcome of this is to bring her to immorality rather than to marriage, for the natural fire will blaze within her and profane her honor. And not this alone, but she will also be a cause to kindle fire in the heart of one who sees and desires, and the land will commit harlotry, and in the end ״the land will be filled with lewdness״ — and so the sin of all the wicked is hung upon his neck. And go forth and learn what I explained in parashat Acharei Mot on the verse (Leviticus 18:2) ״כְּמַעֲשֵׂה אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״ — that the sense of sight magnifies desire for a thing and nullifies the power of the will to refrain, and bends him toward desire for the act — may the Merciful One save us."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:30.367732207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}